      'Ordering is not a problem: each request\'s `custom_id` correlates it with its response. Staying fully synchronous also gives up savings the latency-tolerant jobs could take.',
      'Small batches still have no guaranteed latency; any batch can take up to 24 hours. A merge check that developers wait on needs the synchronous API.',
      'Batches suit non-blocking, latency-tolerant work like nightly test generation and weekly audits, which are single-turn here. Blocking or time-sensitive work stays synchronous, and the savings (about a third) clear the target.',
